{"shortDescription":"The Hunger Games: Sunrise on the Reaping brought audiences back to Panem in force, opening with an estimated $120M domestically and helping lift the overall box office sharply from the prior weekend.Lionsgate’s NYSE:LION latest entry in the franchise debuted at No. 1 from 4,018 locations, averaging…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"i","children":["The Hunger Games: Sunrise on the Reaping"]}," brought audiences back to Panem in force, opening with an estimated $120M domestically and helping lift the overall box office sharply from the prior weekend."]},{"type":"p","children":["Lionsgate’s ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:LION","text":"NYSE:LION"}}," latest entry in the franchise debuted at No. 1 from 4,018 locations, averaging about $29,866 per theater. The film added $105M internationally for a $225M worldwide opening and generated $26.4M globally from IMAX ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:IMAX","text":"NYSE:IMAX"}},", the biggest IMAX debut in franchise history."]},{"type":"p","children":["The broader domestic marketplace collected an estimated $168.08M across 39 reported titles, up 89.5% from the prior weekend but down 8.2% from the comparable 2025 frame, when ",{"type":"i","children":["Wicked: For Good"]}," opened to $147M. The top 10 accounted for about $158.31M. Domestic box-office revenue for 2026 now stands at $8.97B, up 20.4% from the comparable period last year and roughly $1.03B short of $10B."]},{"type":"p","children":["For investors tracking theatrical demand through ticket receipts, the weekend offered a notable rebound ahead of Thanksgiving, even with the launch of Take-Two Interactive’s ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:TTWO","text":"NASDAQ:TTWO"}}," ",{"type":"i","children":["Grand Theft Auto VI"]}," competing for consumers’ entertainment time."]},{"type":"p","children":["Rentrak’s Paul Dergarabedian said speculation that ",{"type":"i","children":["GTA VI"]}," would hurt ",{"type":"i","children":["The Hunger Games"]}," appeared misplaced, arguing that “both can do just fine.”"]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Rocky punches into second"]}]},{"type":"p","children":["Amazon ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:AMZN","text":"NASDAQ:AMZN"}}," MGM Studios’ ",{"type":"i","children":["I Play Rocky"]}," expanded from limited release into 2,477 theaters and collected an estimated $9.33M, good for second place. Its domestic total reached $10.42M. The film also earned an A+ CinemaScore, a rare mark of strong audience approval."]},{"type":"p","children":["Paramount’s ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:SKYD","text":"NYSE:SKYD"}}," ",{"type":"i","children":["Ebenezer"]},", last weekend’s No. 1 film, slipped to third with $7.7M, down about 60% in its second weekend. Its domestic total reached $32.5M, with another $45.9M internationally."]},{"type":"p","children":["Warner Bros.’ ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:SKYD","text":"NYSE:SKYD"}}," ",{"type":"i","children":["The Cat in the Hat"]}," placed fourth with $6.9M, followed by ",{"type":"i","children":["Godzilla Minus Zero"]}," at $2.7M."]},{"type":"p","children":["The remainder of the top 10 was tightly packed. ",{"type":"i","children":["You Can See Everything"]}," and ",{"type":"i","children":["Wild Horse Nine"]}," each collected about $2.5M, followed by Sony’s ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:SONY","text":"NYSE:SONY"}}," ",{"type":"i","children":["Ghost Soldier"]}," at $2.4M, ",{"type":"i","children":["Wildwood"]}," at $2.3M and ",{"type":"i","children":["Ramayana"]}," at $2.1M."]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Thanksgiving next"]}]},{"type":"p","children":["Studios now turn to the five-day Thanksgiving frame, when several new releases will challenge ",{"type":"i","children":["Sunrise on the Reaping"]},". Disney’s ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:DIS","text":"NYSE:DIS"}}," ",{"type":"i","children":["Hexed"]}," and Universal’s ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:CMCSA","text":"NASDAQ:CMCSA"}}," ",{"type":"i","children":["Focker in Law"]}," open wide Wednesday, while Neon expands ",{"type":"i","children":["Paper Tiger"]}," and Netflix ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:NFLX","text":"NASDAQ:NFLX"}}," begins an exclusive IMAX run for ",{"type":"i","children":["The Further Mis-Adventures of Cliff Booth"]},". Angel Studios’ ",{"type":"i","children":["Hershey"]}," opens Thanksgiving Day."]},{"type":"p","children":["Last year’s five-day Thanksgiving period generated $290.31M domestically. The record remains $424.9M from 2024, when ",{"type":"i","children":["Moana 2"]}," contributed $225.44M."]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Top 10 domestic films, Nov. 20-22, 2026"]}]},{"type":"table","children":[{"type":"table-body","children":[{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-header-cell","children":["Rank"]},{"type":"table-header-cell","children":["Film"]},{"type":"table-header-cell","children":["Weekend estimate"]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["1"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"i","children":["The Hunger Games: Sunrise on the Reaping"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["$120.0M"]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["2"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"i","children":["I Play Rocky"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["$9.33M"]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["3"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"i","children":["Ebenezer"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["$7.7M"]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["4"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"i","children":["The Cat in the Hat"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["$6.9M"]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","